---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { allQuestions, allPapers } from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="About this site" context="about" description="Who runs chemistryaleveltutor.com and where the questions, mark schemes and ratings come from.">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p>chemistryaleveltutor.com is run by {site.company}, an A-level tutoring business with a small team of specialist tutors. The site exists to give OCR, AQA and Edexcel chemistry students the past-paper material they actually use, sorted the way they revise, free and without sign-up; and to introduce students who want more help to a tutor who teaches the OCR specification every week.</p>
  <h2>Where the material comes from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Questions, mark schemes and examiner comments</strong> are from the exam boards' own published papers. The OCR section has every Chemistry A series since June 2016 (H032 AS from 2016, H432 A level from 2017): {allPapers.length} papers and {allQuestions.length.toLocaleString()} question parts. The <a href="/aqa/">AQA section</a> has every AQA Chemistry series over the same years (7404 AS from 2016, 7405 A level from 2017) and the specimen papers: 50 papers and 2,306 question parts. The <a href="/edexcel/">Edexcel section</a> has every Pearson Edexcel Chemistry series over the same years (8CH0 AS from 2016, 9CH0 A level from 2017): 47 papers and 2,042 question parts. Each part has been tagged to the specification statements it assesses, its maths skills and practical work, and its question type. Where a part needs a table, graph or structure printed in an earlier part of the question, that earlier part folds out above it.</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty ratings</strong> (Easy, Medium, Hard) come from the wording of OCR's examiners' reports on each part. OCR's reports do not give facility figures, and parts the report does not discuss are left unrated.</li>
    <li><strong>Key-term cards and topic notes</strong> are written by our tutors and are original; nothing derived from OCR's material is generated automatically.</li>
    <li><strong>Grade boundaries and exam dates</strong> are OCR's, AQA's and Pearson's published figures.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>The tutoring is by Laraib, a practising medical doctor who tutors A-level Chemistry for every exam board, including OCR A, AQA and Edexcel; see the <a href="/tutors/">tutor page</a>. The site is built and maintained by the same small team that runs <a href="https://www.alevelbiologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelbiologytutor.com</a>, <a href="https://www.mathsaleveltutor.com" rel="noopener">mathsaleveltutor.com</a> and <a href="https://www.alevelpsychologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelpsychologytutor.com</a>.</p>
  <h2>Mistakes</h2>
  <p>If you find one, tell us on the <a href="/report/">report a mistake</a> page; corrections usually go live the same week.</p>
</Base>
